e Hinojosa at only about 23-24% despite tight polling", "Expert ratings cluster at Lean R, with one Likely R and one Tossup"], "rationale": "Recent polling puts the race within a point or two, but Abbott's incumbency, massive financial advantage, and the markets' roughly 77% Republican pricing justify keeping him favored beyond the raw poll average. The consensus of raters at Lean R matches a small but real Republican edge.", "watch": "Turnout composition in early voting, especially among the suburban and young voters polls show breaking toward Hinojosa, could close the gap further.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Greg Abbott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Texas governor is closer than usual this cycle. Incumbent Republican Greg Abbott seeks another term against Democratic state Representative Gina Hinojosa, and recent surveys from Marist, YouGov, Siena, and UT/Texas Politics show the race essentially tied, with an average margin of about two points for Abbott. Several October polls even show Hinojosa narrowly ahead.\n\nStill, Abbott holds major structural advantages: he has raised $25 million with $67 million on hand, dwarfing Hinojosa's $6 million raised, and most expert ratings place the race at Lean R. Prediction markets give Democrats only about a one-in-four chance. The race is competitive but tilts Republican heading into early voting.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1819, "margin": -4.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2694, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2894, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2702, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -3.3}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2978, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2717, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2616, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2625, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0